-- title:
--   Injectivity of the e-th power map between crossing models
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring, let $\pi \in W$ be arbitrary, and let $e$ be a natural number with $e \neq 0$. Write $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,t$ for the quotient of the ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ of formal power series in two variables (indexed by `Fin 2`) by the ideal generated by the single element $X_0X_1 - t$, where $t \in W$ is viewed in $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ via the constant coefficient map, and write $\mathrm{mk}\,t$ for the quotient ring homomorphism onto it. The assertion is that there exists a $W$-algebra homomorphism $$\theta \colon W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \pi^e) \longrightarrow W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \pi)$$ with two properties: first, for every two-variable power series $F$ over $W$, the image under $\theta$ of the class of $F$ in the source equals the class in the target of `MvPowerSeries.expand e he F`, the power series obtained from $F$ by substituting $X_i^{\,e}$ for each variable $X_i$; second, $\theta$ is injective. Only existence is asserted, and no hypothesis is imposed on $\pi$, on the invertibility of $e$ in $W$, on completeness of $W$, or on the presence of $e$-th roots of unity in $W$.
--
--   This is the $e$-th power (or $\mu_e$-covering) map $u \mapsto x^e$, $v \mapsto y^e$ identifying the $A_{e-1}$ crossing model $W[[u,v]]/(uv - \pi^e)$ with a subring of the $A_0$ model $W[[x,y]]/(xy - \pi)$, in the form used for the local structure of degenerate fibres of modular curves. It is cited by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_powMap_range_eq_fixedPoints`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_powMap_range_eq_fixedPoints), which identifies the image of $\theta$ with the $\mu_e$-fixed part of the target.
-- source:
